Plan edits:

1. In walkUp: add `let restarts = 0;` and `let expectKey: string | null = null;` plus a pageKey helper.

Helper:
```ts
/** 지금 화면의 카드 줄. 창을 닫고 돌아왔을 때 목록이 다른 자리로 되돌아갔는지 견줄 때 쓴다. */
function pageKey(xml: string): string {
	const parsed = parseSalesDump(xml);
	return parsed.ok ? parsed.cards.map((card) => card.title).join("|") : "";
}
```

2. Loop body beginning: after parsing, check expectKey.

```ts
		const xml = settledXml(serial, exec);
		const nodes = parseNodes(xml);
		const parsed = parseSalesDump(xml);
		const key = parsed.ok ? parsed.cards.map((card) => card.title).join("|") : "";
		// 창을 닫고 돌아오면 목록이 맨 위로 되돌아가기도 한다(2026-11-07 실기). 처리하던 자리가 아니면 맨 아래부터 다시 걷는다.
		if (expectKey !== null) {
			const moved = key !== expectKey;
			expectKey = null;
			if (moved) {
				if (restarts >= MAX_WALK_RESTARTS) break;
				restarts += 1;
				scrollToEdge(serial, exec, ops, "bottom");
				prev = "";
				stuck = 0;
				page = 0;
				continue;
			}
		}
```

3. In card loop after done handling:

Replace:
```ts
				// 끌어올린 글은 목록 맨 위로 옮겨 가 화면 배치가 바뀐다. 이 덤프의 나머지 카드는 믿지 않고 다시 읽는다.
				if (done === "bump") {
					reread = true;
					break;
				}
```
with:
```ts
				// 창을 닫으면 목록 배치가 바뀐다(끌어올린 글은 맨 위로, 돌아오면 화면이 맨 위로). 이 덤프의 나머지 카드는 믿지 않고 다시 읽는다.
				expectKey = key;
				reread = true;
				break;
```

4. Remove the later duplicate key computation (reuse `key`).

Also add MAX_WALK_RESTARTS const.

One issue: after processing all cards in a page without action (no pending there), we swipe back. Fine.

Another: when `reread` triggered and expected key equal, we then process whole new dump from top — card already deleted from pending, fine.

Potential infinite loop safety: restsarts bounded, turn bounded by 60.

Detecting "moved": for price-only on a list that rewinds to top too. Good.

But a concern: bump success → list changes → restart from bottom. Each restart re-scans from bottom. With 6 items and each bump causing a restart, that's 6 restarts. MAX restarts maybe 12. And turn limit 60 — a restart consumes 1 turn, fine.

Wait, also possible: after successful bump the list doesn't rewind (only dialog close resets?). In real device the dialog close may or may not rewind; either way key changes since the bumped card left its position? Actually bumped card moves to top of the list — if the visible page doesn't contain it after the move... the page content likely changes. If not changed, we continue fine.

Hmm, but there's a subtle inefficiency: even a successful bump whose page key doesn't change → no restart. OK.

Set MAX_WALK_RESTARTS = 8? For 6 items each with restart, plus maybe. Use 12.

Let me apply the edits.

